@startuml seq-vault-grant
title Credential exchange: vault → HMAC grant → hand pull (as deployed)

actor User
participant "andromeda" as tui
participant "serve" as serve
participant "Secret Manager" as sm
participant "hand h-<sid>" as hand
participant "GitHub / upstream" as ext

== 1. store (user-owned) ==
User -> tui : cred set gh-token
tui -> serve : PUT /v1/credentials/gh-token\nBearer apl_… + {"value":"ghp_…"}\n<color:#CC0000><b>cleartext over HTTP (F2)</b></color>
serve -> sm : create/addVersion\nid = agentplane-cred-<user>-gh-token\n<color:#CC0000>ambiguous concatenation (F8)</color>
note right of sm : value never returned by the API afterwards

== 2. session create → grant ==
User -> serve : POST /v1/sessions {"agent":"starter"}
serve -> serve : names = templateCredentials(agent)\ngrant = HMAC(sid,user,names,exp=<b>now+10min</b>)\n<color:#007700>key = AGENTPLANE_GRANT_KEY, serve-only (F3 fixed)\nTTL 10 min (F4 fixed)</color>
serve -> hand : POST /admin/grant  {serveBase, grant, credentials}\nBearer HAND_ADMIN_TOKEN <color:#CC0000>(still shared by every hand)</color>
note right of hand : no secret VALUE in this message — only the grant

== 3. hand pulls the value ==
hand -> serve : GET /v1/hand/credentials/gh-token\nBearer <grant>
serve -> serve : verifyGrant: HMAC + exp only\n<color:#CC0000>not bound to the calling actor (F3)</color>
serve -> sm : access(user, name)
sm --> serve : {"type":"git","token":"ghp_…"}
serve --> hand : 200 payload
hand -> hand : write ~/.git-credentials (0600)\n<color:#CC0000>now inside the sandbox & its snapshots (F6)</color>

== 4. use ==
hand -> ext : env / header credential, from actor memory
note over hand, ext #FFE4E4
  This path remains for <b>env</b> and <b>header</b> credentials, and the value
  is in actor memory — so it is in the snapshot (<b>F6</b>: checkpoints capture
  memory pages, not only disk).
end note

== GIT no longer uses any of the above ==
hand -> hand : url."http://git-proxy/gh/".insteadOf https://github.com/
hand -> ext : plain HTTP to git-proxy, carrying only the <b>grant</b>
note over hand, ext #E4FFE4
  <b>Deployed (2026-08-04).</b> git-proxy exchanges the grant for the user's
  token OUTSIDE the sandbox and re-originates over HTTPS. The token never
  enters the actor, so no checkpoint can capture it. No TLS is terminated and
  no CA is provisioned into the sandbox — which is what stalled the general
  gateway. Extending this to env/header credentials is the remaining F6 work.
end note
@enduml
